Frequently Asked Questions

What engine does the Jaguar XE 2.0d use?
The XE 2.0d uses the AJ200D 2.0-litre inline-four diesel engine, part of Jaguar's Ingenium family. It was fitted from 2015 to 2016.

How much does a Jaguar XE 2.0d engine rebuild cost?
Rebuilds start from £2,000. Exact price depends on condition and parts required — submit your reg for a fixed-price quote.

Which engine code is fitted to my XE 2.0d?
Your XE 2.0d has the AJ200D diesel engine. Enter your registration on this page and we'll confirm your exact spec and provide a quote.

Do you rebuild AJ200D XE 2.0d engines?
Yes. We replace the timing chain, injectors, EGR and gaskets as standard on every AJ200D rebuild.

Do you supply used XE 2.0d engines?
Yes, in some cases a matched low-mileage used engine is the right option. Our team will advise honestly once we've matched your registration and understood your situation.

Can you recover my XE 2.0d if the engine has failed?
Yes — nationwide recovery is available from £70, and most vehicles are collected within a few hours of booking.

How long does an XE 2.0d engine rebuild take?
Most rebuilds are completed within 3-5 working days from the time your car arrives at our workshop.

Is rebuilding better than fitting a used engine?
For most XE 2.0d owners, yes. A rebuild removes the compatibility risk that comes with an unknown used unit's history, and comes with a 12-month unlimited-mileage warranty — often longer and more comprehensive than what a used engine supplier offers.

